{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1087", "sample_idx": 35, "model_name": "abacusai/dracarys-llama-3.1-70b-instruct", "content": "the social network is a film that has been widely acclaimed for its portrayal of the founding of facebook and the subsequent rise of its creator, mark zuckerberg. the movie is based on the book \"the accidental billionaires\" by ben mezrich, and it tells the story of how zuckerberg, a sophomore at harvard university, created a website that would eventually become one of the most popular social networking sites in the world.\n\nthe film begins with zuckerberg, played by jesse eisenberg, as a socially awkward and introverted computer science major who is desperate to gain acceptance into one of harvard's exclusive final clubs. after being dumped by his girlfriend, erica albright, played by rooney mara, zuckerberg creates a website called \"facemash,\" which allows users to compare the photos of two students and vote on which one is more attractive. the site becomes a huge success, but it also attracts the attention of the university's administration, who shut it down and put zuckerberg on academic probation.\n\ndespite the setback, zuckerberg is approached by a group of students, including cameron and tyler winklevoss, who are impressed by his programming skills and ask him to help them create a social networking site called \"harvard connect.\" however, zuckerberg has other plans and decides to create his own site, which he calls \"thefacebook.\" with the help of his friend and fellow student eduardo saverin, played by andrew garfield, zuckerberg launches the site, which quickly becomes a huge success.\n\nas thefacebook gains popularity, zuckerberg and saverin become embroiled in a dispute with the winklevoss twins, who claim that zuckerberg stole their idea. the dispute eventually leads to a lawsuit, which is settled out of court. meanwhile, zuckerberg's relationship with saverin deteriorates, and the two friends have a falling out.\n\nt